virglrenderer: Venus pass views live while the pass is open

What: image views get a serial (the one count render passes and framebuffers use,
moved to vkr_common.c). A framebuffer keeps its views by id and serial; an imageless
begin and vkCmdBeginRendering leave theirs with the command buffer until the pass
ends. A begin whose framebuffer view was destroyed, and a next subpass or end after
the app destroyed one of the open pass's views, are refused: the app's context ends
(its command buffer is invalid).
Why: Mesa's vk_render_pass reads the framebuffer's (or an imageless begin's) views at
the begin, at each next subpass and at the end, and KosmicKrisp reads a rendering's
at its end (its resolves): a view destroyed while recording was freed memory there.
Not covered (ADR 0065, still open): KosmicKrisp also reads a pass's resolve views
where it splits the pass inside (barriers, compute), and views or images destroyed
under a recorded or pending command buffer.
Upstream: OmacVM policy (object lifetime VUIDs).
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-commands.c (the c-state-destroyed-view- cases, also
under libgmalloc); --time: microseconds per vkCmdBeginRenderPass + vkCmdEndRenderPass.

